---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';

const effective = 'August 22, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Forger Digital Solutions handles information on its public website."
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Privacy Policy</span>
  </nav>
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="doc__updated">Last updated: {effective}</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="doc__lead">
      Forger Digital Solutions ("FDS", "we", "us") builds software and publishes this website as
      an independent studio. We aim to collect as little personal information as possible. This
      policy explains what that means in practice.
    </p>

    <div class="doc__body">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This website is a static, informational site. It does not use cookies or analytics,
        does not run advertising or trackers, and does not ask you to create an account or
        submit personal information to browse it.
      </p>

      <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. Like most web hosts, GitHub may automatically log
        technical information — such as your IP address, browser type, and the pages requested —
        for security and operational purposes. That data is handled by GitHub under its own
        privacy practices, not by FDS.
      </p>

      <h2>Information you choose to send us</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>,
        we receive whatever you include — typically your email address and message. We use it only
        to respond to you and keep it no longer than needed. Our email is provided by Google
        (Gmail) and is subject to Google's privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party links and services</h2>
      <p>
        The site links to external services we use, including GitHub, YouTube, Discord, Ko-fi, and
        Cash App. If you follow those links or interact with those services, their own privacy
        policies apply — we do not control them and are not responsible for their practices.
      </p>
      <p>
        Support contributions for FDS development and hardware are handled entirely by Ko-fi and
        Cash App. FDS does not receive or store your payment card details; any payment information
        is processed by those services and their providers. If you email FDS about a hardware
        donation, we use the details you choose to send only to coordinate that donation.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
        information from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Because we don't maintain accounts or a marketing database, there's little for you to
        manage. If you've emailed us and would like your message deleted, just ask.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the site evolves. When we do, we'll revise the "last updated"
        date above.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email
        <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.supportEmail}`}>{siteConfig.supportEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a class="doc__back" href="/">&larr; Back home</a>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc__back { display: inline-block; margin-top: 3rem; font: 700 .76rem/1 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
</style>
